r=Path.cwd();p=r/'tools/build-guides.py';s=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8-sig')
user=[
'An entity relationship (ER) diagram shows tables as boxes and declared foreign keys as arrows. Choose Database ER diagram in the upper-right page selector after opening the intended project or cache. DPH uses captured SQL table and key metadata. It never connects to a database server or executes target SQL. Empty results mean no matching supported captured declarations, not proof that the application has no database.',
'Read PARTIAL schema above the drawing. Its counts show matching tables, related foreign keys, omitted relationships, source gaps and unresolved foreign keys. Blue arrows connect captured exact table targets; orange dashed arrows mark unresolved relationships when both endpoints are available. Missing or off-page targets remain in the FK evidence selector without an invented box or line. Cardinality, deployed enforcement, referenced uniqueness, type compatibility and effective migration order are unverified.',
'Each table box shows ordered column names and declared types. PK means primary key, FK means foreign key and UQ means unique key. These badges describe captured column membership. A repeated membership appears once per badge. Orange table borders mark gaps, duplicates or a truncated column summary. The footer reports shown and total columns. Click a table to read its full captured columns, keys and gaps in the labeled details memo below the drawing. Open evidence selects that exact table in Database schema, including its required page.',
'To inspect an arrow, scroll the command strip sideways to the FK evidence selector and choose its numbered entry. The memo shows the original key, ordered local and referenced columns, source hash, capture generation and source range. Open evidence selects the exact key in Database schema. Arrow numbers correspond to selector entries. The selector retains relationships touching a visible table even when the other endpoint is outside the focus, page or filter.',
'For a smaller diagram, select a table, column or key in Database schema, then click View ER diagram in that page\'s command strip. Alternatively click Focus schema selection in the ER command strip. Focus includes that exact table and its directly linked incoming and outgoing neighbors. The text filter searches table name, schema and source within that focus. All tables clears both focus and text. First page resets paging; Next page advances by the selected 15, 30 or 60 table page size. Zoom offers 75 through 200 percent; use the drawing scrollbars to reach enlarged cards and lower rows.',
'The default IDE-editable cards summarize seven columns; all captured columns remain available in table evidence. A page holds at most 60 tables and 120 related foreign-key entries. Omitted FK counts are explicit. Duplicate table declarations stay separate; inferred SQL references, views and unsupported statements do not become table entities. The diagram is regenerated when a capture is replaced. In a small window, scroll commands sideways, scroll the drawing independently and drag the details divider if needed. Maximize the window for the largest useful diagram.',
'For exact launch, practice and build steps, read docs/guides/Database_ER_Diagrams_Run_and_Test.txt. The controlled fixture contains ER_Customers, ER_Orders and ER_Lines with two arrows. Focus ER_Orders to see that three-table chain. ER_ManyLinks deliberately exercises the relationship display limit. Inspect SelfRef and MissingRef for self links and unresolved evidence. These diagrams are rendered by the running native application, not mockup screens.'
]
engineering=[
'TDPHDatabaseSchema.Diagram projects independent JSON from the existing captured schema inventory. Only declared table headers become nodes. IDs, exact ownership, source SHA256, generation and source ranges survive projection. Owned columns retain order, declared types, nullability and resolved local key membership badges. Duplicate badge kinds are condensed. No source, owner catalog or persisted workspace is changed.',
'Captured foreign keys become numbered edges with exact key, owner and referenced table IDs, ordered members and referenced columns, source provenance and relationship state. A solid blue line requires complete captured key links and both visible table endpoints. Unresolved captured links with available endpoints draw orange dashed lines. Missing targets receive no invented ID or ghost node. Relationships touching either visible endpoint remain in the evidence selector when the other endpoint is filtered or off page. Arrow direction runs from the referencing table to the referenced table; no crow-foot cardinality is inferred.',
'Focus uses the selected declaration ID and a one-hop incoming/outgoing neighbor set. It does not expand transitively. Text filtering applies after focus and stable inventory order is retained across pagination. Bounds require a nonnegative offset, 1 to 60 tables and 1 to 32 summarized columns; native page choices are 15, 30 and 60. The projection retains at most 120 related foreign keys with total and omitted counts. Duplicate names, owned gaps, unresolved keys, absent columns and truncated summaries mark node notes and orange card borders. Global qualification remains PARTIAL CAPTURED SCHEMA even for supported individual declarations.',
'DatabaseERTab and all command, scroll, memo and style controls are serialized in DPH.UI.Main.fmx for the IDE Object Inspector. The existing Main unit paints the data using a native canvas; it does not construct runtime controls or introduce a helper unit. Table size, header height, column row height, gutters, margins, fonts, colors and zoom controls are editable form properties. DatabaseERRect arranges stable table cards in a grid; orthogonal FK routes use outside-card gutters, arrowheads and selector numbers, including self links. The canvas resizes for content and magnification. Defaults summarize seven columns.',
'Table hit testing and FK selection retain exact evidence IDs. Open evidence clears schema filters and navigates to the correct 250-row inventory page. Focus accepts a selected table or the declaration owner of a column/key/gap. Capture loading rebuilds the projection and resets stale focus/evidence IDs; empty results explain recovery. Drawing and details scroll independently, commands scroll horizontally, and a serialized splitter adjusts evidence space. Open source remains subject to the existing generation/hash guards on the schema page.',
'Run tools/build-database-er.cmd elevated. The suite captures real project SQL resources and checks projection ownership, badge membership, provenance, stable order, limits, missing/duplicate/self targets, focus, filtering, paging, immutable source/catalog/workspace and SQLite reopening. Native tests exercise card selection, exact evidence navigation across pages, the serialized page selector, zoom, compact scrolling and capture replacement; screenshots include the full native canvas and actual window. Fixtures use the fixed ignored bin/database-er-validation folder. Run stored-object and key regressions and tools/build-wp0.cmd for the actual application/FM X resource baseline.',
'The visualization proves supported captured structure, not a live schema, SQL semantic validation or business meaning. Dialect validity, effective migration order, referenced uniqueness, type compatibility, cardinality and deployed enforcement remain unverified. Views and inferred usage references remain schema evidence rather than invented entities. Source gaps and display limits stay visible. No target SQL, target application or database server is executed.'
]
